WEBVTT

00:00:04.820 --> 00:00:08.760
Puzzle No. J-22-E: released.

00:00:09.970 --> 00:00:12.820
J-85-V: released.

00:00:14.040 --> 00:00:16.950
J-99-G: released.

00:00:18.520 --> 00:00:21.790
J-207-H: released.

00:00:22.660 --> 00:00:24.540
This concludes my report.

00:00:24.810 --> 00:00:27.040
Unbelievable, isn't it?

00:00:27.040 --> 00:00:28.280
These Philosopher's Puzzles.

00:00:28.280 --> 00:00:29.920
Four, one after the other.

00:00:29.920 --> 00:00:31.480
And single-handedly.

00:00:32.010 --> 00:00:34.260
A Solver from Root Gakuen, eh?

00:00:34.260 --> 00:00:36.010
Correct.

00:00:36.480 --> 00:00:39.350
The one who released all
these puzzles is THIS man:

00:00:39.350 --> 00:00:41.220
Kaito Daimon.

00:00:41.220 --> 00:00:43.370
He holds a pact
with the Armlet of Orpheus.

00:00:44.550 --> 00:00:46.900
This idiotic-looking fellow?

00:00:47.430 --> 00:00:50.820
What of the abilities
awakened by the pact?

00:00:50.820 --> 00:00:53.610
We have no definite information yet.

00:00:54.110 --> 00:00:59.700
But it appears he does not yet have
complete control over them.

00:01:00.110 --> 00:01:04.960
More precisely, he seems
to want to reject the pact.

00:01:06.090 --> 00:01:10.180
Reject abilities given
only to the chosen one?!

00:01:10.180 --> 00:01:12.380
Could it be he actually IS an idiot?

00:01:12.380 --> 00:01:17.020
It is extremely doubtful that this person
is befitting the armlet.

00:01:17.020 --> 00:01:19.560
Then let's test him.

00:01:20.370 --> 00:01:23.030
We have investigated his past.

00:01:23.030 --> 00:01:25.180
And the perfect puzzles with which to test him.

00:01:25.790 --> 00:01:28.640
We shall ascertain for
ourselves, Kaito Daimon...

00:01:32.110 --> 00:01:34.990
We'll see if you have what
it takes to be a Phi-Brain.

00:01:53.610 --> 00:01:55.920
Kimi no nounai e to shinnyuu
Gonna infiltrate your brain

00:01:55.920 --> 00:01:58.650
Nemutteru suki ni baby, open the gate
While you're sleeping, baby, open the gate

00:01:58.650 --> 00:02:00.500
Fukuzatsusugi security
Too-complicated security

00:02:00.500 --> 00:02:03.240
Kakusareru to abakitakunaru
When something's hidden, it makes me want to expose it

00:02:03.240 --> 00:02:07.750
Barabara ni chirabatte iru password o hiroiatsume
I'll gather up those loose, scattered passwords

00:02:07.750 --> 00:02:12.460
Kakushin ni sematte yuku, sono shoutai o misete
And approach the core, so show me that true form

00:02:12.460 --> 00:02:14.680
Kantan ni clear dekinai
I can't clear it easily

00:02:14.680 --> 00:02:17.330
Saki nante motto yomenai
Can read what lies ahead even less

00:02:17.330 --> 00:02:19.340
Kaidoku fukanou smile
A smile that can't be deciphered

00:02:19.340 --> 00:02:21.640
Kiken na puzzle
A dangerous puzzle

00:02:21.640 --> 00:02:23.580
Lock sareteta door aru nara
If there's a door that's been locked

00:02:23.580 --> 00:02:26.400
Zutto tataite miru beki, kaza-ana hiraku wa
You must keep striking it, a crack will open

00:02:26.400 --> 00:02:30.900
Eien ni hodokenai nazo nanka wa nai
No mystery remains unsolved forever

00:02:30.900 --> 00:02:33.200
Makiokosu, it's a supernova!
It's forming, it's a supernova!

00:02:33.200 --> 00:02:37.890
Tobikiri shigekiteki na hirameki o agemashou
I will give you thoroughly stimulating insight

00:02:37.890 --> 00:02:40.110
Misskey-misskey la-tu-ma

00:02:40.110 --> 00:02:42.450
Yume no naka, it's a supernova!
In the middle of a dream, it's a supernova!

00:02:42.450 --> 00:02:45.080
Watashi wa, sou, brain diver
I am, yes, a brain diver

00:02:45.080 --> 00:02:50.970
Kimi ga sagashimotometeru kotae ni nareru made
Until I become familiar with the answer you seek

00:02:53.630 --> 00:02:56.650
Brain diver

00:02:58.380 --> 00:03:01.450
Brain diver

00:03:06.060 --> 00:03:09.960
Invitation from a Nightmare

00:03:12.780 --> 00:03:14.460
"Genius Terrace"?

00:03:14.790 --> 00:03:17.330
Yeah. The cafeteria's Terrace No. 1 has

00:03:17.330 --> 00:03:20.170
become a meeting place
for students with titles.

00:03:20.920 --> 00:03:23.720
Why do they let those guys
get away with so much?

00:03:23.720 --> 00:03:25.780
What are the principal and

00:03:25.780 --> 00:03:27.310
student council president thinking?

00:03:27.510 --> 00:03:30.080
A private space where you
can eat all you want.

00:03:30.080 --> 00:03:31.980
Must be nice!

00:03:32.730 --> 00:03:34.480
Genius Terrace, huh?

00:03:35.110 --> 00:03:38.280
Sure enough, students
with titles are awesome!

00:03:38.280 --> 00:03:40.320
Nothing but a bunch of weirdoes!

00:03:40.770 --> 00:03:44.030
Excellent, Kaito! You're
displaying excellent brainwaves.

00:03:44.200 --> 00:03:46.720
I, Ana, am inserting a lighthouse here.

00:03:46.720 --> 00:03:47.810
Do what you like.

00:03:50.310 --> 00:03:51.670
Thanks for the food!

00:03:51.670 --> 00:03:52.960
Thanks!

00:03:53.830 --> 00:03:55.820
I got tripped up by the leeks!

00:03:55.820 --> 00:03:57.210
I win!

00:03:57.210 --> 00:03:58.160
I didn't lose to YOU!

00:03:58.160 --> 00:03:59.770
It's the leeks! I lost to the leeks!

00:03:59.770 --> 00:04:01.380
You're a hell of a poor sport!

00:04:01.380 --> 00:04:02.680
You just thank the leeks!

00:04:02.680 --> 00:04:04.790
Nothing but weirdoes, but

00:04:04.790 --> 00:04:07.100
they're great at puzzles,
if nothing else.

00:04:09.710 --> 00:04:12.260
Kaito. I made these cookies in Home Ec.

00:04:12.260 --> 00:04:13.810
Nonoha sweets!

00:04:13.810 --> 00:04:15.230
"Nonoha sweets"?

00:04:15.700 --> 00:04:17.200
Don't get close. They're dangerous!

00:04:17.200 --> 00:04:19.070
What the heck? How rude!

00:04:19.070 --> 00:04:20.480
Have you forgotten?!

00:04:24.710 --> 00:04:25.780
<i>There you are.</i>

00:04:27.720 --> 00:04:28.840
<i>Nonoha.</i>

00:04:30.130 --> 00:04:33.000
<i>Here. I made these for you, Kaito.</i>

00:04:33.360 --> 00:04:35.260
<i>Eat these and cheer up.</i>

00:04:36.130 --> 00:04:37.420
<i>Thank you.</i>

00:04:48.710 --> 00:04:49.790
<i>What's the matter?</i>

00:04:50.920 --> 00:04:52.930
<i>Kaito? Hey!</i>

00:04:53.170 --> 00:04:58.060
<i>Was it good? It was good, right? Kaito!</i>

00:04:58.060 --> 00:05:00.440
<i>Kaito! Hey, Kaito!</i>

00:05:00.960 --> 00:05:03.030
That really was a close one.

00:05:03.340 --> 00:05:04.970
My, don't make me blush.

00:05:04.970 --> 00:05:07.590
They were so delicious that you stopped crying.

00:05:07.590 --> 00:05:08.780
No frickin' way!

00:05:09.480 --> 00:05:13.540
I got no interest in some
girl's cooking, but all right:

00:05:13.540 --> 00:05:14.950
Want ME to have a taste?

00:05:14.950 --> 00:05:16.120
Here, Cube, have a taste.

00:05:16.820 --> 00:05:18.560
-<i>She ain't listenin'!</i>
-That's Cubik Galois.

00:05:18.560 --> 00:05:20.520
Call me by my proper name.

00:05:20.520 --> 00:05:22.080
See? They're good, right?

00:05:22.080 --> 00:05:24.880
Yes. Not bad, Nonoha.

00:05:24.880 --> 00:05:26.090
Why's he looking DOWN on me?

00:05:26.700 --> 00:05:28.430
Getting along well, aren't you?

00:05:28.740 --> 00:05:30.050
Upperclassman Jikukawa!

00:05:30.050 --> 00:05:33.430
Da Vinci, Galileo, Edison, and Einstein.

00:05:33.750 --> 00:05:36.050
Geniuses with titles.

00:05:36.050 --> 00:05:37.530
I hope you'll continue to work together,

00:05:37.530 --> 00:05:39.170
and to challenge these puzzles.

00:05:39.170 --> 00:05:40.440
You're kiddin', right?

00:05:40.440 --> 00:05:42.440
I don't intend
to hang out with these guys.

00:05:42.440 --> 00:05:43.870
Huh?!

00:05:43.870 --> 00:05:45.940
Then why are you here every day?

00:05:46.470 --> 00:05:48.760
Could it be you really
like these people?

00:05:48.760 --> 00:05:49.990
All of them?

00:05:49.990 --> 00:05:52.850
No way! I just like the view here.

00:05:53.780 --> 00:05:55.180
What's that?

00:05:59.250 --> 00:06:00.770
POG?

00:06:17.720 --> 00:06:19.510
Kaito Daimon, correct?

00:06:21.230 --> 00:06:26.130
I am Bishop, a Giver with POG Japan's
Central Tactical Office.

00:06:26.600 --> 00:06:30.760
I have come for you, the
pact holder of Orpheus.

00:06:31.630 --> 00:06:36.120
We hold your abilities
in the highest regard.

00:06:36.120 --> 00:06:38.420
I wished to see you just
once, for the future's sake,

00:06:38.420 --> 00:06:40.980
and to have some questions answered.

00:06:40.980 --> 00:06:44.770
Such was the idea of POG
Japan's chief officer.

00:06:45.740 --> 00:06:48.660
Is the principal up to something again?

00:06:48.660 --> 00:06:51.180
No. Something like this
wouldn't be possible.

00:06:52.530 --> 00:06:53.930
What do you say?

00:06:54.260 --> 00:06:56.160
You shouldn't do it.

00:06:56.160 --> 00:06:58.180
It's... dangerous somehow.

00:06:58.450 --> 00:07:01.890
Rest easy: We are not such
an uncouth organization

00:07:01.890 --> 00:07:04.180
as to cause people harm.

00:07:04.720 --> 00:07:06.780
Aside from puzzles, you mean. Right?

00:07:10.070 --> 00:07:11.360
Fine. I'll go.

00:07:11.360 --> 00:07:12.200
Kaito!

00:07:12.200 --> 00:07:15.400
There's a ton of things I
have to say to the guys who

00:07:15.400 --> 00:07:17.490
get off making piece-of-shit deadly puzzles!

00:07:17.490 --> 00:07:19.460
Then I'm going, too.

00:07:19.460 --> 00:07:20.680
And me, too!

00:07:20.680 --> 00:07:21.700
Why?

00:07:21.700 --> 00:07:24.500
I've got somethin' to say
to this "chief officer" guy:

00:07:24.900 --> 00:07:28.340
If you want these Philosopher's Puzzles solved,
come talk to ME!

00:07:29.190 --> 00:07:31.840
Very well. Your classmates may come, too.

00:07:32.040 --> 00:07:35.090
I'm not going. I hate airplanes.

00:07:35.090 --> 00:07:37.350
Me, neither. I'm not done drawing.

00:07:54.060 --> 00:07:55.840
How far do you think we'll go?

00:07:55.840 --> 00:07:57.530
Hey, POG dude!

00:07:57.900 --> 00:07:58.700
Yes?

00:07:58.700 --> 00:08:01.240
What is a "pact holder of Orpheus"?

00:08:01.700 --> 00:08:04.920
It is the one chosen by
the Armlet of Orpheus.

00:08:04.920 --> 00:08:06.280
Armlet?

00:08:06.280 --> 00:08:08.130
The Armlet of Orpheus is said

00:08:08.130 --> 00:08:10.730
to stimulate the human brain to its

00:08:10.730 --> 00:08:14.190
utmost limit, and to
awaken latent abilities.

00:08:14.670 --> 00:08:19.680
However, those abilities will differ
depending on the person.

00:08:19.870 --> 00:08:21.630
It's really that amazing?

00:08:21.630 --> 00:08:22.690
So this guy solved

00:08:22.690 --> 00:08:25.020
the puzzles
thanks to that armlet?!

00:08:25.020 --> 00:08:25.960
Wanker!

00:08:25.960 --> 00:08:27.200
Not at all.

00:08:27.200 --> 00:08:30.290
The armlet would not choose
one with no gift for puzzles.

00:08:30.290 --> 00:08:33.200
It is because he has the power
to challenge the Philosopher's Puzzles

00:08:33.200 --> 00:08:35.200
that even we in the POG

00:08:35.200 --> 00:08:39.000
consider Kaito Daimon this
generation's greatest Solver.

00:08:39.630 --> 00:08:41.660
That's why puzzles keep
going only to Kaito?

00:08:41.660 --> 00:08:44.660
Sheeit! Why some guy who
can't even eat leeks?

00:08:44.660 --> 00:08:46.030
Leave leeks outta this!

00:08:46.030 --> 00:08:47.960
Enough! Stop fighting!

00:08:48.260 --> 00:08:51.950
I never thought the POG would come
directly to the school...

00:08:52.380 --> 00:08:54.990
So you knew nothing about this?

00:08:54.990 --> 00:08:58.720
Knowing all of the POG's
movements is impossible.

00:08:59.270 --> 00:09:02.320
I am a school principal, nothing more.

00:09:02.320 --> 00:09:04.810
What if something should happen to them?

00:09:04.810 --> 00:09:06.210
If they cannot overcome it,

00:09:06.210 --> 00:09:08.900
then such was
the extent of their abilities.

00:09:10.670 --> 00:09:12.530
The experiment's a success.

00:09:12.690 --> 00:09:15.540
Without a doubt, the
micro-machine for observing

00:09:15.540 --> 00:09:18.030
Kaito works even from long distances.

00:09:18.640 --> 00:09:20.040
You're not getting away.

00:09:22.630 --> 00:09:24.250
Looks like we're here, huh?

00:09:28.660 --> 00:09:31.960
This is POG Japan's laboratory.

00:09:31.960 --> 00:09:33.460
It's so big!

00:09:33.700 --> 00:09:35.680
The history of the Philosophers' Puzzles

00:09:35.680 --> 00:09:37.720
is the history of battles between Givers and Solvers.

00:09:38.650 --> 00:09:42.690
Here, information on puzzles
from the past is collected,

00:09:42.690 --> 00:09:46.230
and new puzzles are created each day.

00:09:46.230 --> 00:09:47.920
Oh! Look at that!

00:09:47.920 --> 00:09:48.730
Huh?

00:09:48.730 --> 00:09:50.290
"Puzzle of God"?

00:09:50.290 --> 00:09:51.670
Puzzle of God, huh?

00:09:51.670 --> 00:09:53.230
So that's what POG meant.

00:09:57.640 --> 00:10:00.370
Welcome to the POG.

00:10:04.330 --> 00:10:06.540
A facility like this, underground...

00:10:06.650 --> 00:10:08.820
My apologies for the long trip.

00:10:08.820 --> 00:10:11.330
Up ahead, three puzzles have been

00:10:11.330 --> 00:10:13.710
arranged for your amusement.

00:10:13.710 --> 00:10:16.260
I hope you find them satisfying.

00:10:18.630 --> 00:10:22.870
The chief executive
awaits you just ahead.

00:10:23.540 --> 00:10:25.980
I wish you good luck.

00:10:26.350 --> 00:10:29.460
Meetin' the big cheese
comes with a price, huh?

00:10:29.460 --> 00:10:30.980
How friggin' stingy!

00:10:34.410 --> 00:10:38.200
So this is the first
puzzle. A disc tower, huh?

00:10:42.650 --> 00:10:45.040
Puzzle time... Begin.

00:10:52.700 --> 00:10:54.550
What's a disc tower?

00:10:54.650 --> 00:10:56.540
You turn the dics and line up the rows

00:10:56.540 --> 00:11:00.120
so the same color ain't repeated in the columns.

00:11:02.410 --> 00:11:04.640
I'LL solve this puzzle!

00:11:04.640 --> 00:11:07.490
I gotta appeal to the big cheese and

00:11:07.490 --> 00:11:09.560
show him what I can do!

00:11:10.170 --> 00:11:12.850
That armlet of yours
picked the wrong guy!

00:11:12.850 --> 00:11:14.170
Do what you like.

00:11:14.170 --> 00:11:17.110
I did so many of these puzzles
over there that I'm sick of 'em.

00:11:17.410 --> 00:11:18.440
"Over there"?

00:11:18.920 --> 00:11:21.740
Kaito studied abroad in England.

00:11:21.740 --> 00:11:23.410
At the Crossfield Academy.

00:11:23.410 --> 00:11:25.100
Huh? Cross...?

00:11:25.100 --> 00:11:27.660
That famous school
where all the geniuses go?!

00:11:28.300 --> 00:11:30.000
This moron went there?

00:11:30.000 --> 00:11:32.170
The principal made that decision for me.

00:11:32.170 --> 00:11:32.670
Huh?!

00:11:33.970 --> 00:11:36.620
The principal's your friggin' guardian?!

00:11:37.490 --> 00:11:40.450
I never knew you bastards were like that!

00:11:40.450 --> 00:11:42.930
That's why you get special treatment, huh?

00:11:42.930 --> 00:11:46.140
No way! If anything, he's
been a giant pain in the ass!

00:11:46.140 --> 00:11:48.560
Hey, don't say that!

00:11:48.560 --> 00:11:51.540
You were on your own,
and he took you in, didn't he?!

00:11:51.540 --> 00:11:52.480
On your own?

00:11:54.880 --> 00:11:55.610
Nonoha!

00:12:08.130 --> 00:12:09.720
Thank you.

00:12:13.100 --> 00:12:14.160
Ow...

00:12:14.160 --> 00:12:16.020
Be careful, for cryin' out loud.

00:12:16.020 --> 00:12:17.150
Yeah, sorry.

00:12:19.070 --> 00:12:20.300
It opened.

00:12:20.300 --> 00:12:21.550
So that's how it works, huh?

00:12:21.550 --> 00:12:22.950
On to the next one!

00:12:24.410 --> 00:12:26.810
This is called a disc tower?

00:12:38.170 --> 00:12:39.780
Stonehenge...

00:12:41.060 --> 00:12:42.850
What kind of puzzle is it this time?

00:12:42.850 --> 00:12:45.500
We gotta make all the
stones be at equal height.

00:12:47.090 --> 00:12:48.750
Kaito? What's the matter?

00:12:48.750 --> 00:12:50.290
Uh, well...

00:12:50.290 --> 00:12:51.600
The hell?

00:12:51.600 --> 00:12:53.580
You did this "over there" as well?

00:12:53.580 --> 00:12:54.460
Yeah.

00:12:54.800 --> 00:12:56.340
In that case,

00:12:56.340 --> 00:13:00.350
you can watch as I solve this puzzle
oh-so-friggin' elegantly.

00:12:57.870 --> 00:12:59.100
What's going on?

00:12:59.100 --> 00:13:00.100
Kaito?

00:13:00.160 --> 00:13:01.510
They ain't lookin'!

00:13:13.710 --> 00:13:15.210
Dammit, be careful!

00:13:15.690 --> 00:13:17.910
But it just suddenly...

00:13:31.490 --> 00:13:32.880
All right, let's go!

00:13:32.880 --> 00:13:34.080
What're you mad about?

00:13:34.080 --> 00:13:36.490
I ain't mad at nothin'!

00:13:42.880 --> 00:13:44.260
The Tower of Hanoi.

00:13:44.830 --> 00:13:46.120
Polycube.

00:13:46.120 --> 00:13:47.760
Tangram.

00:13:47.760 --> 00:13:51.390
These are all puzzles I liked long ago.

00:13:52.400 --> 00:13:54.160
Is it a coincidence?

00:13:54.160 --> 00:13:56.540
Or was this route purposefully...?

00:14:01.840 --> 00:14:04.360
Who chose this route?

00:14:05.500 --> 00:14:07.540
What do they know about me?

00:14:10.760 --> 00:14:13.040
We're here. The final puzzle.

00:14:13.760 --> 00:14:16.040
Wanna do this next one yourself?

00:14:16.340 --> 00:14:18.110
No. That's fine.

00:14:18.110 --> 00:14:20.090
Huh? Oh...

00:14:20.560 --> 00:14:23.510
What's inside there?

00:14:50.250 --> 00:14:52.570
It can't be... Right?

00:14:57.150 --> 00:14:59.610
What kind of puzzle is this?

00:14:59.610 --> 00:15:01.080
I'll take some notes.

00:15:01.570 --> 00:15:03.350
Three glowing rectangles?

00:15:03.350 --> 00:15:04.550
What are they?

00:15:04.550 --> 00:15:05.850
There's more over there.

00:15:07.070 --> 00:15:08.060
They move!

00:15:08.060 --> 00:15:10.430
If we fell, it would be bad.

00:15:10.430 --> 00:15:12.430
Take care, for real!

00:15:14.070 --> 00:15:15.930
Huh? It fell!

00:15:16.060 --> 00:15:18.310
And one of them stopped glowing.

00:15:19.490 --> 00:15:21.310
Oh! Four of them did.

00:15:21.760 --> 00:15:23.190
I get it.

00:15:23.190 --> 00:15:24.740
When we reach the goal and

00:15:24.740 --> 00:15:28.140
all of them stop glowing,
that door will open, huh?

00:15:28.140 --> 00:15:29.040
Really?

00:15:29.040 --> 00:15:30.060
Probably.

00:15:30.060 --> 00:15:31.280
"Probably"?

00:15:31.820 --> 00:15:35.030
Look, just keep quiet and
stick with me, Nonoha!

00:15:37.540 --> 00:15:40.080
These plates move the same
way as ladder lotteries.

00:15:40.080 --> 00:15:41.240
Ladder lotteries?

00:15:41.800 --> 00:15:43.080
Oh! You're right!

00:15:43.080 --> 00:15:46.480
The bars on the plates ahead
will all go out and fall,

00:15:46.480 --> 00:15:48.360
no matter how many of 'em are glowing.

00:15:48.360 --> 00:15:51.720
But the plates we ride,
just one of the bars will stop glowing.

00:15:52.830 --> 00:15:54.470
Yup, that's it for sure!

00:15:58.070 --> 00:15:59.360
Why?

00:16:00.810 --> 00:16:03.520
Why is this puzzle here?

00:16:06.400 --> 00:16:08.020
This way next!

00:16:22.460 --> 00:16:24.360
Another four stopped glowing, huh?

00:16:24.360 --> 00:16:25.750
Over there next!

00:16:25.750 --> 00:16:29.210
Hey! You don't have to pull me so hard,
I'm following you!

00:16:30.220 --> 00:16:32.450
Uh, it's not like I
wanted to hold yer hand

00:16:32.450 --> 00:16:34.210
strongly or anythin' like that.

00:16:34.210 --> 00:16:36.210
Huh? Anyway, we sure have gone

00:16:36.210 --> 00:16:38.790
back-and-forth a lot, huh?

00:16:38.790 --> 00:16:41.110
Just makin' the lights
go out isn't enough.

00:16:41.110 --> 00:16:42.860
We gotta make all the plates drop,

00:16:42.860 --> 00:16:45.340
all the lights go out,
AND arrive at the goal,

00:16:45.340 --> 00:16:46.550
so this the only route.

00:16:46.550 --> 00:16:47.970
You really are a genius!

00:16:49.400 --> 00:16:51.360
You may praise me more!

00:17:03.080 --> 00:17:04.020
Come on, this way!

00:17:04.020 --> 00:17:04.830
O-Okay.

00:17:11.780 --> 00:17:14.840
<i>Father. Mother.</i>

00:17:22.590 --> 00:17:24.980
<i>This is... This is...!</i>

00:17:28.090 --> 00:17:29.060
A puzzle!<i></i>

00:18:01.910 --> 00:18:04.600
If I... If I...

00:18:05.580 --> 00:18:08.520
If I'd realized it was
a puzzle sooner...!

00:18:11.040 --> 00:18:12.860
I thought we were done for!

00:18:12.860 --> 00:18:15.660
I saw right through that trick.

00:18:15.660 --> 00:18:17.100
Kaito!

00:18:19.270 --> 00:18:22.470
I don't... don't want to see them again!

00:18:22.470 --> 00:18:24.040
Stupid puzzles!

00:18:24.040 --> 00:18:27.120
Just go away!

00:18:31.870 --> 00:18:35.490
Run amuck... Escaped, eh?

00:18:39.150 --> 00:18:39.810
Kaito!

00:18:39.810 --> 00:18:41.950
Hey, wait! You wanna fall again?!

00:18:41.950 --> 00:18:44.390
But I have to get to Kaito!

00:18:44.390 --> 00:18:46.890
Fine. Let's hurry and clear this!

00:19:04.050 --> 00:19:05.910
Okay, solved it!

00:19:08.160 --> 00:19:09.580
Kaito!

00:19:13.420 --> 00:19:16.170
Hey! Why won't it open?! Damn!

00:19:17.280 --> 00:19:18.940
Are you okay, Kaito?

00:19:18.940 --> 00:19:21.180
Stupid puzzles... Stupid puzzles!

00:19:21.180 --> 00:19:23.170
They should all go away!

00:19:24.380 --> 00:19:26.170
Jeez, what the heck's goin' on?

00:19:26.170 --> 00:19:28.590
Hey, why are you holdin'
onto her, damn you?!

00:19:28.590 --> 00:19:31.930
I'm sorry! Father, Mother.

00:19:31.930 --> 00:19:33.990
Because of me...

00:19:36.070 --> 00:19:37.350
This puzzle...

00:19:43.320 --> 00:19:48.540
It might have something to do with
how Kaito's parents died.

00:19:53.760 --> 00:19:55.420
What should we do?

00:19:55.420 --> 00:19:57.970
A shock! Give him a strong shock!

00:19:57.970 --> 00:19:58.820
You two bastards!

00:19:58.820 --> 00:19:59.880
Hurry up and do it!

00:20:00.290 --> 00:20:03.020
But what should I do?

00:20:04.150 --> 00:20:06.430
I can't "shock" him, but these cookies...

00:20:06.800 --> 00:20:09.130
That's it! Nonoha sweets!

00:20:09.130 --> 00:20:11.260
That will be a strong shock!

00:20:11.260 --> 00:20:13.110
Huh? No, these are delicious cookies-

00:20:13.110 --> 00:20:13.940
Give 'em!

00:20:16.050 --> 00:20:18.190
Look! Nonoha sweets!

00:20:19.690 --> 00:20:20.690
C'mon!

00:20:20.930 --> 00:20:23.370
How is it, Kaito? Is it good?

00:20:26.150 --> 00:20:27.950
M-Murderer.

00:20:27.950 --> 00:20:29.200
He's back to normal!

00:20:29.200 --> 00:20:31.460
That's some serious trauma.

00:20:31.460 --> 00:20:32.470
How cruel!

00:20:32.470 --> 00:20:34.710
I think they're delicious, Nonoha.

00:20:34.710 --> 00:20:36.710
It was good, right?! Hey!

00:20:36.920 --> 00:20:39.630
-Hey! Say it was good!

00:20:38.600 --> 00:20:39.630
-She ain't listenin'.

00:20:40.470 --> 00:20:44.490
<i>Unfortunately, given that
Kaito Daimon has collapsed,</i>

00:20:44.490 --> 00:20:47.200
further discussion is considered impossible.<i></i>

00:20:47.200 --> 00:20:50.430
<i>Thus, today's talks are hereby suspended.</i>

00:20:50.430 --> 00:20:51.520
What?!

00:20:51.520 --> 00:20:54.650
<i>Everyone, you will be
taken back to the school.</i>

00:20:55.500 --> 00:20:57.170
<i>Please, this way.</i>

00:20:59.470 --> 00:21:02.770
Oh, that's nice. Getting
back will be a breeze.

00:21:02.770 --> 00:21:04.530
Well, it can't be helped.

00:21:04.900 --> 00:21:08.530
More to the point, how'd
you bastards get here?

00:21:08.930 --> 00:21:09.700
With this.

00:21:09.700 --> 00:21:11.600
Hey! My bike?!

00:21:11.600 --> 00:21:13.350
Thanks to you, we made it in time.

00:21:13.870 --> 00:21:15.160
You okay?

00:21:15.160 --> 00:21:16.310
Yeah.

00:21:17.550 --> 00:21:19.500
What was with those guys?

00:21:19.500 --> 00:21:21.070
What were they trying to do?

00:21:21.070 --> 00:21:22.620
Pitiful, huh?

00:21:22.620 --> 00:21:25.970
Relivin' some dumb-ass trauma-drama!

00:21:22.620 --> 00:21:25.970
["Tiger and Horse": A goofy word play, combining the Japanese words
Tiger (tora) + Horse (uma) into the English word Trauma (torauma)]

00:21:25.970 --> 00:21:29.020
You prick, you blew our one good chance!

00:21:29.020 --> 00:21:30.240
Gammon!

00:21:30.240 --> 00:21:31.590
You think this is about you?!

00:21:31.590 --> 00:21:32.930
Kaito.

00:21:33.220 --> 00:21:35.440
Try undoing this puzzle ring.

00:21:35.440 --> 00:21:38.270
Huh? The hell? Jeez.

00:21:42.530 --> 00:21:45.390
What's goin' on? I
should be able to solve

00:21:45.390 --> 00:21:47.780
a puzzle like this in three seconds!

00:21:48.310 --> 00:21:49.680
I can't solve it.

00:21:51.650 --> 00:21:54.570
Kaito? What's the matter?

00:21:54.570 --> 00:21:58.100
The principal's bad feeling
was accurate, huh?

00:21:58.590 --> 00:22:02.960
Your brain is causing a
counter-reaction to puzzles.

00:22:03.300 --> 00:22:07.020
At this rate, you'll never be
able to solve puzzles again.

00:22:07.890 --> 00:22:10.360
I... can't do puzzles?!

00:22:14.390 --> 00:22:17.920
Ethics. Common sense. Emotion.

00:22:18.670 --> 00:22:20.700
Unless all these are transcended,

00:22:20.700 --> 00:22:22.980
one cannot become a Phi-Brain.

00:22:24.810 --> 00:22:28.040
Nor can one challenge the Puzzle of God.

00:22:37.290 --> 00:22:41.510
Tsukue no ue de umareta sekai
A world born on top of a desk

00:22:41.510 --> 00:22:47.430
Ichiban saki ni kimi ni misetakatta
I wanted to show it to you first of all

00:22:47.430 --> 00:22:52.060
Karappo no heya sotto nukedashite
I sneaked silently out of that empty room

00:22:52.060 --> 00:22:57.110
Hashirihajimeteta
And started running

00:22:58.270 --> 00:23:02.590
Iki hazumasete oka o noboru to
Breathing heavily, I climbed the hill

00:23:02.590 --> 00:23:07.950
Kimi ga saki ni tsuite matte ita ne
And you were already there, waiting

00:23:08.820 --> 00:23:13.130
Takusan no hajimete kimi to mitsuketa
There were so many treasures that I first

00:23:13.130 --> 00:23:18.380
Takaramono datta
Discovered with you

00:23:18.380 --> 00:23:23.720
Kanashisa de afureta toki wa
That time when I was overcome with sadness

00:23:23.720 --> 00:23:26.400
Nanimo iwazu ni tada
You said nothing

00:23:26.400 --> 00:23:29.310
Soba ni ite kureta ne
Just stayed there by my side, didn't you?

00:23:29.310 --> 00:23:33.880
Imademo wasurenai yo
Even now, I haven't forgotten

00:23:33.880 --> 00:23:39.180
Mata aou ne, yakusoku o shiyou
Let's meet again, let's make it a promise

00:23:39.180 --> 00:23:44.460
Kei wa shinai, ano hi no sayonara
It won't fade, the "goodbye" of that day

00:23:44.460 --> 00:23:50.000
Boku no subete, kimi ga kureta michi
Everything I have, the path you gave me

00:23:50.000 --> 00:23:58.940
Zutto kokoro no naka hikaru yo
Will always shine within my heart

00:24:03.560 --> 00:24:05.380
I wonder if Kaito's all right.

00:24:05.380 --> 00:24:08.040
Gammon, how do you think
we can cheer him up?

00:24:08.040 --> 00:24:10.210
There ain't no need to cheer him up!

00:24:10.210 --> 00:24:14.180
Starting now, MY puzzle time will begin!

00:24:14.180 --> 00:24:18.690
I feel sort of anxious...
I'm going to go see Kaito!

00:24:18.690 --> 00:24:20.390
Gammon, finish things for me.

00:24:20.390 --> 00:24:22.910
Next time: "Resurgence Toward the Light"

00:24:21.830 --> 00:24:27.250
Resurgence Toward the Light

00:24:22.910 --> 00:24:26.320
Hey, hold on! Ain't I bein'
treated kinda roughly?!
